  "scope": "New C++/Python full-region Boolean APIs combine complete pixel-grid area geometry beyond the image canvas. Union/XOR admit a full envelope; intersection and subtraction avoid distant spans. Ordered manager-row preparation preserves saved rows and source words while publishing current/Previous selection without pixel history. Borrowed geometry/storage admission precedes owned captures and callbacks; operands, controls and source guards freeze before execution. ROI Manager automatically uses full geometry for regional operands, and explicit full mode handles legacy vectors through editor actions/live Python handles. Scientific publication uses the native metadata controller. The detached Python model keeps intrinsic bitmap extent and origin. Existing canvas APIs and legacy-only default manager combinations remain unchanged. This does not complete continuous ShapeRoi path storage, rotation, creation/modifier commands or portable recorded Boolean workflow integration.",
