    "reference": "New observations from unchanged ImageJ 1.54r sources/classes comprise 144 two-stage pixel-region groups (288 stages) plus 40 mixed vector/packed groups (80 stages). Inputs include off-image coordinates, holes, disconnected populations, empty states and repeated operations. Expected membership and bounds come from actual ShapeRoi algebra. Pixel-cell input regions are materialized through ImageJ ThresholdToSelection, so this is pixel-membership evidence, not continuous composite-path retention. Existing fixtures, historical runs and Auto expectations remain unchanged.",
    "actual_ui": "Real dock-tab and Ctrl-row pointer input selects two saved regional operands and clicks Union in the shared ImGui ROI Manager. The result retains 21 cells with only 8 visible on the canvas, preserves saved rows and source words, captures Previous and adds no pixel history. Sixteen standalone regressions run, including scientific-manager input paired with the Python launch and twelve saved budget/pointer/modifier recipes. This is not OS-input or new regional standalone-launch certification.",
    "failed_attempts": "Initial compile lacked the roi_style declaration include. The first new mixed-input test used the public legacy from_dict decoder for a nested-attribute vector fixture; corrected only test construction, preserving oracle observations. End-to-end scientific integration then exposed both the existing action allowlist and legacy adapter read-only commit route; metadata-only Boolean actions now use the established native-controller route. The retained preimage module/source and failing smoke logs record those refusals. The new manager test also assumed a visible field that this control schema does not expose; it now checks manager visibility, enabled controls and resulting state. No original tests, fixtures or historical expectations were changed."
